Import from `@/components/ui/storage`. `StorageBrowser` is fully controlled: it shows buckets in a sidebar and the open bucket's files with search, sort, selection, and drop-to-upload, while the host owns the buckets, objects, selection, query, sort, folder path, uploads, and every action. It fetches nothing, checks no permissions, and doesn't filter or sort `objects`, so pass them already matched to `query` and ordered by `sort`.

It fills its parent, so give the parent a bounded height:
```tsx
'use client';
import { useState } from 'react';
import { StorageBrowser, type ObjectSort, type StorageBucket, type StorageObject } from '@/components/ui/storage';

const buckets: StorageBucket[] = [{ id: 'b1', key: 'avatars', visibility: 'public', isPublic: true, allowCustomKeys: false }];
const objects: StorageObject[] = [{ id: 'o1', bucketId: 'b1', key: 'a.png', filename: 'a.png', mimeType: 'image/png', size: 20480, isPublic: true, createdAt: '2026-10-01T09:00:00Z' }];

export function Files() {
  const [bucketId, setBucketId] = useState<string | null>('b1');
  const [selectedIds, setSelectedIds] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [sort, setSort] = useState<ObjectSort>({ column: 'createdAt', direction: 'desc' });
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('');
  return (
    <div className="h-[640px]">
      <StorageBrowser
        buckets={buckets} selectedBucketId={bucketId} onSelectBucket={setBucketId}
        objects={objects.filter((o) => o.bucketId === bucketId && (o.filename ?? o.key).includes(query))}
        selectedIds={selectedIds} onSelectionChange={setSelectedIds}
        sort={sort} onSortChange={setSort} query={query} onQueryChange={setQuery}
        onOpenObject={openDetails} onUpload={pickFiles} onDropFiles={upload}
        onDownload={download} onDelete={(o) => remove([o.id])} onBulkDelete={remove}
      />
    </div>
  );
}
```
`sort` is `{ column: 'filename' | 'size' | 'createdAt' | 'mimeType', direction: 'asc' | 'desc' }`.

- `selectedBucketId` (string | null): with none chosen the pane asks for a bucket. `onNewBucket()`, `busyBucketId` (spinner on that row), and `bucketsSelectable` (default true) shape the sidebar.
- Row actions, each `(object) => void` and hidden when omitted: `onOpenObject`, `onDownload`, `onCopyLink`, `onRename`, `onDelete`.
- Folders: rows with `kind: 'folder'` open through `onOpenFolder(object)`; `segments: { label, path }[]` adds a breadcrumb, and `onNavigate(path | null)` gets null for the bucket root.
- Upload: `onUpload()` adds the header button, `isUploading` disables it, and `onDropFiles(files: FileList)` makes the list a drop target.
- Selection: `selectable` (default true), `onBulkDelete(ids)`, `bulkDeleteProgress: { done, total, failed: string[] }`, `onClearSelection()`.
- States: `isLoading`, `emptyLabel` (empty-list text, e.g. no matches), and `emptyState`: `'empty-bucket'` keeps the header, while `'no-buckets' | 'no-access' | 'not-provisioned'` fill the pane; its buttons call `onEmptyStateAction` / `onEmptyStateSecondaryAction`.
- `title` (default "Storage"), `defaultSidebarCollapsed`, `framed`, `locale`, `className`.

Render these beside it: `ObjectDetailSheet` (`object: StorageObject | null`, `open`, `onOpenChange(open)`, `onDownload?`, `onCopyLink?`, `onRename?(id, newName)`, `onDelete?(id)`; image previews read `object.downloadUrl`), `BucketConfigSheet` (`mode: 'create' | 'edit'`, `initial?`, `open`, `onOpenChange`, `onSubmit(value)` with the bucket's editable fields), and `UploadDropzone` (`onFiles(files)`, `uploads?: { id, filename, size, progress, status: 'queued' | 'uploading' | 'done' | 'error' }[]`, `onCancel?(id)`).

Import from `@/components/ui/agents-builder`. A complete agent workspace (chat, inbox, schedules, integrations, skills, and an agent view with a live run) that renders only what `data` holds: the block owns navigation between its views, the connect dialog, and scripted playback; the host owns the data, routing, OAuth, persistence, and every action it reports.

It fills its parent, so give the parent a bounded height:
```tsx
'use client';
import { AGENTS_BUILDER_DEMO, AgentsBuilder, type AgentsBuilderData } from '@/components/ui/agents-builder';

// The type is large: spread the demo and replace what you have.
const data: AgentsBuilderData = {
  ...AGENTS_BUILDER_DEMO,
  workspace: { name: 'Acme', appName: 'Acme' },
  agents: [{ id: 'revenue-analyst', name: 'Revenue Analyst', running: true }],
};

<div className="h-dvh">
  <AgentsBuilder
    data={data}
    onAuthorizeIntegration={(integration) => startOAuth(integration.id)}
    onConnectIntegration={(integration, toolIds) => saveConnection(integration.id, toolIds)}
    onAction={(action) => {
      if (action.type === 'open-agent') router.push(`/agents/${action.agentId}`);
    }}
  />
</div>
```
`data` holds `workspace` (`{ name, appName }`), `models`, `integrations` (`{ id, name, description, vendor, authDomain, connected, tools: { id, name, access: 'read' | 'write' }[] }`), `categories`, `featuredIntegrationIds`, `agents` (`{ id, name, running? }`), `inbox`, `schedules`, `clock`, `skills`, `starterPacks`, `recommendations`, `fallbackReply`, `followUpReply`, `agent` (the agent view's blueprint), `run`, `heroHighlights`, and `usage: { percent }`.

Chat is scripted and sends nothing to the host: a recommendation plays its `reply`, a first typed message plays `fallbackReply`, and later ones play `followUpReply`. For a chat answered by a live model, build it from the `ai` item's transcript and composer instead.

- `view` / `defaultView` / `onViewChange(view)`: `'chat' | 'inbox' | 'schedules' | 'integrations' | 'skills' | 'agent'`, default `'chat'`.
- `onAuthorizeIntegration(integration) => Promise<void>` runs the connect dialog's sign-in step: resolve to move on to choosing tools, reject to go back. Without it the dialog waits a moment and moves on.
- `onConnectIntegration(integration, toolIds: string[]) => void | Promise<void>` saves the connection; reject to keep the dialog open. Once it resolves the integration shows as connected (tracked locally, seeded from each `connected` flag).
- `onAction(action)` gets every control the block doesn't own: `navigate { target: 'usage' | 'settings' | 'more-agents' }`, `open-agent { agentId }` (`data.agent.id` opens the built-in view instead), `new-agent`, `search { query }`, `workspace-menu { item: 'organization' | 'profile' | 'support' | 'whats-new' | 'log-out' }`, `workspace-mode { mode: 'agents' | 'workbench' }`, `chat-history`, `attach-file { surface: 'chat' | 'run' }`, `send-follow-up { surface: 'run', text }`, `stop-run`, `approve-run { agentId, approved }`, `send-reply { threadId, text, drafted }`, `approve-thread-action { threadId }`, `new-schedule`, `toggle-schedule { scheduleId, active }`, `run-schedule { scheduleId }`, `share-agent` / `edit-instructions` / `set-identity { agentId }`, `request-app`, `manage-integration { integrationId }`, `create-skill`, `browse-skill-library`, `add-starter-pack { packId }`, `open-skill { skillId }`, `create-agent { draft: { name, schedule, integrationIds, steps } }`.
- `theme` / `onThemeChange` (`'light' | 'dark' | 'system'`) only drive the menu's appearance switch; apply the theme yourself.
- `defaultSidebarCollapsed`, `framed` (a rounded window on a canvas), `autoplayRun` (default true; false opens the run settled), `className`.

Import from `@/components/ui/sheets`. A metadata-driven CRUD grid: it reads a table's columns from the endpoint's `_meta`, then loads, edits, creates, and deletes rows itself over GraphQL with the host's session. There's no `data` prop and no save callback. The host owns the endpoint, the session token, and auth errors, and PostgreSQL privileges and RLS at the endpoint decide every read and write.

Render it in a client component. `Sheets` fills its parent, so give the parent a bounded height, and mount `<PortalRoot />` from `@/components/ui/portal` once as the last child of `<body>` for the overlay editors:
```tsx
'use client';
import { useMemo } from 'react';
import { Sheets, SheetsProvider, type SheetsConfig } from '@/components/ui/sheets';

export function ProjectsGrid({ endpoint, userId, getToken }: { endpoint: string; userId: string; getToken: () => string | null }) {
  const config = useMemo<SheetsConfig>(
    () => ({ endpoint, auth: { mode: 'embedded', getToken, getIdentityKey: () => userId }, onAuthError: signOut }),
    [endpoint, getToken, userId],
  );
  return (
    <SheetsProvider config={config}>
      <div className="h-[680px] min-h-0">
        <Sheets tableName="Project" pageSize={25} />
      </div>
    </SheetsProvider>
  );
}
```
`tableName` is a table's `name` in `_meta`, its GraphQL type name. To let people pick one, call `useSheetsMeta()` inside the provider, pass `data?._meta?.tables ?? []` to `selectConsoleDataTables` from `@constructive-io/data`, and give the names to `<SheetsTableSelector tables={names} activeTable={name} onTableChange={setName} isLoading={isLoading} />`.

`SheetsProvider` takes `config: SheetsConfig`; keep it referentially stable.
- `endpoint` (the app GraphQL endpoint) and `auth` are required. `auth` is `{ mode: 'embedded', getToken: () => string | null, getIdentityKey?: () => string | null }`, where the identity key is a non-secret user id that keeps each user's cache apart, or `{ mode: 'standalone' }` with `authEndpoint` and the grid wrapped in `SheetsAuthGate` from `@/components/ui/sheets/auth`.
- Optional: `databaseId`, `locale` (default en-US), `fieldTypeOverrides: Record<string, string>`, `upload: { bucketKey? }` (default "public"), `queryClient` (reuse yours), `onAuthError()` (on a 401, before the error throws), `onError(error, { source?: 'grid' | 'editor' | 'mutation' | 'upload', tableName? })`, `logger`, `plugins`.
- To replace the transport: `execute(document, variables?)`, `executeUpload(file, path?, options?) => Promise<{ url }>`, or a whole `adapter: SheetsBackendAdapter` (`fetchMeta`, `listRows`, `createRow`, `updateRow`, `deleteRow`).

`Sheets` props:
- `tableName` (required), `pageSize` (default 100), `showSelection` and `showPagination` (default true), `infiniteScroll` (default false), `className`.
- Observers only, since the grid does its own writes: `onRowSelect(rows)`, `onCellEdit(id, field, value)` once an edit is saved (`id` is the primary key, or an object for a composite key), and `onEvent({ type, tableName, at, meta? })` with `type` load:success | load:error | cell:edit | row:create | row:delete | filter:apply | sort:change | page:change.
- `slots: { toolbar?, empty?, error?({ error, retry }), loading? }` replace those regions; `cellTypes` and `cellSlots` customize cells; `commands`, `keymap`, `interceptors`, and `onCommand(event, result)` extend or observe grid commands; `theme` and `themeMode` ('light' | 'dark' | 'system') style it.
- A `ref` gets `SheetsHandle`: `scrollToRow(index)`, `submitDrafts()`, `refetch()`, `getSelectedRows()`, `exportCsv({ columns?, filename? })`.

## Usage

Pass an adapter that binds each call to the signed-in account. The block owns the add, text-a-code, verify, and remove flow; the host owns requests, credentials, and error codes.

```tsx
import {
  AccountPhoneNumbers,
  type AccountPhoneNumbersAdapter
} from '@/blocks/account/account-phone-numbers/account-phone-numbers';

const adapter: AccountPhoneNumbersAdapter = {
  list: () => api.listPhoneNumbers(),
  add: ({ number }) => api.addPhoneNumber(number),
  sendCode: ({ number }) => api.sendPhoneVerificationCode(number),
  verify: ({ number, code }) => api.verifyPhone(number, code),
  remove: ({ id }) => api.removePhoneNumber(id)
};

<AccountPhoneNumbers adapter={adapter} identityKey={session.userId} />
```

Numbers are E.164. Throw `AccountPhoneNumbersUnavailableError` when the backend has no phone support, and an error with a `code` (or GraphQL `extensions.code`) to show the matching entry from `messages.errors`. Compose `useAccountPhoneNumbers` with `AccountPhoneNumbersView` when you need to own the layout or state.

## Usage

Create one registry for the application, adapt navigation at the host boundary, and render the palette near the root layout. Pages can register commands while mounted with `usePageCommands`.

```tsx
import { createCommandRegistry, kbd } from '@constructive-io/command-palette';
import { CommandPalette } from '@/blocks/command-palette/command-palette';

const registry = createCommandRegistry({
  groups: [{ id: 'navigation', label: 'Navigation', priority: 1 }],
  commands: [{
    id: 'settings',
    label: 'Open settings',
    type: 'navigation',
    group: 'navigation',
    href: '/settings',
    shortcut: kbd(',', 'mod')
  }]
});

<CommandPalette registry={registry} navigate={(href) => router.push(href)} />;
```

The installed block owns presentation and keyboard interaction. The headless package owns command registration, execution, multi-step state, and background-task lifecycle. Route authorization, action permissions, errors, and business workflows remain the host application's responsibility.
